{
  "name": "Pantheon",
  "_about": "THE PANTHEON at its real size, from the engine's primitives. The rotunda is 43.3m across inside and as high to its crown, so a sphere would fit it: a wall 6.2m thick in layers. Inside, the order: six exedrae each screened by a pair of Corinthian columns carrying an entablature round the room (broken over the entrance and the apse opposite it), eight aediculae between them -- a podium, two columns, a pediment -- and above, the attic zone with a blind window in every bay, up to the springing. The dome is a hemisphere with the 9m oculus, five rows of twenty-eight coffers sunk along the line of sight from the middle of the floor. Outside, two cornices band the drum and three step rings hold the dome's haunches. In front, the intermediate block (the door through it, flat on top) and the portico on its three steps: eight Corinthian columns 14.15m tall across the front, two rows of four behind making three aisles, the entablature and its cornice, and the low pediment.",
